# TactiQ OS 2.0.0 — Production Image SELinux Enforcing Boot Log
# Date: 2026-07-17
# Hardware: Rock 5A (RK3588S), 4 GiB LPDDR4X
# Image: tactiq-image (production, no root shell)
# Policy: refpolicy-targeted v2.7.0 (cleansstate rebuild)
# Tag: v2.0.0-rc6 (tactiq-os: 776d6f7, tactiq-os-selinux: ce3e6f9)
# Note: image built from 776d6f7, before the rc6 release commit (8cc8d83).
#       Difference: DISTRO_VERSION string only. The boot banner reads
#       "TactiQ OS 2.0.0" — this confirms the DISTRO_VERSION defect
#       that was fixed in the release commit.
# Kernel: 6.18.24-yocto-standard
# Result: ZERO AVC denials on the boot path to login prompt. SELinux enforcing
#         from init (audit timestamp 1.364s); policy load at audit 1.520s
#         (156ms after enforcing; 158ms by printk clock 1.371630 -> 1.529396).
#         Scope limit: proven is zero AVC among all visible audit records plus
#         the first suppression window at 5.403s (21 callbacks), fully
#         accounted for by seq numbering (visible 1-10, then 32 = 21 hidden).
#         The second window at 20.679s (76 callbacks, 36 seq numbers missing
#         -> multi-record events) surrounds a failed root login and is NOT
#         accounted for; AVC in 7-20s cannot be excluded from this log.
#         Boot reached multi-user well before it, so the boot-path claim holds.
#         Seq 37 is absent between visible 36 and 38 and is covered by no
#         suppression message - unexplained.
#         Side observation: the failed root login is itself positive evidence
#         that the production image has no shell by design.
#         For a suppression-free artifact: rerun with kernel.printk_ratelimit=0
#         in bootargs (extlinux.conf, edited offline) and no login attempt.
#         RAUC good-marking under enforcing: mount/unmount of p4 (rootfs_b),
#         p1 (boot_a), p3 (boot_b); active root p2 (rootfs_a) mounted at
#         boot (1.188s), remounted ro (3.051s), not released.
#         All systemd units reached OK.
#
# Capture method: UART (CP2102, 1500000 baud, PuTTY COM3)
# ---

